B.aY6=new A.aF(B.aYT,["A student reads only comments that support an initial opinion, then checks a source that disagrees.","A practice quiz feels easy today; a later review checks whether the idea can still be explained.","A brief reply could mean several things; the setting and earlier events may change its meaning.","One observation can support a possibility without proving it; new evidence may shift the conclusion.","A reviewer writes down a first impression, then actively checks for a counterexample.","A deadline encourages a fast choice; a reversible step can preserve time to check missing facts.","Frustration can signal that something matters while leaving the best next action open to review."],t.li)
